Package: kelixip-mod-auth-db
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: Emmanuel BUU <emmanuel.buu@ives.fr>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Section: net
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://www.ives.fr/
Depends: kelixip (= @VERSION@)
Description: Database authentication module for kelixip
 Digest authentication against a MariaDB/MySQL subscriber table
 (kamailio-compatible ha1/ha1b columns): it owns the challenge/accept/reject
 decision, the scripts only compose the SIP response. Enable it with a
 [module.auth_db] block in config.toml.
 .
 The module's registered name is auth_db (the [module.auth_db] block); the
 package is named kelixip-mod-auth-db because a Debian package name may not
 contain an underscore. The RPM is kelixip-mod-auth_db.
 .
 The payload is BEAM bytecode, but the package is architecture-dependent on
 purpose: it must be built and shipped alongside the core whose embedded ERTS
 will load it.
